In 2027, CHY3 moves from a tool platform to a co-creation platform. The AI Co-Creation Suite is not a chat box bolted onto the product. It is a set of models integrated into the places where creative work actually slows down.

# Four surfaces

A copy engine drafts product descriptions, launch notes, and localized variants. A design assistant proposes palettes, layout directions, and rapid visual variations. A code assistant is tuned for CreaSDK APIs, so integration work takes an afternoon instead of a sprint. A market analyst reads the ValueFlow pipeline and surfaces growth opportunities, anomalies, and audience shifts.

# Context is the advantage

Generic AI tools do not know the project, the revenue data, or the audience. The suite does. Its suggestions can be specific: this pricing page loses people at the third step; this audience responds to a different promise; this content format has the best retention per hour invested.

# Rollout

The first beta arrives in Q1 2027, starting inside IdeaForge with the copy and design modules. Code and market analysis follow as the data layer matures.
